  "summary": "HTTP::Body versions before 1.24_02 for Perl parse the trailer in quadratic time.",
  "details": "HTTP::Body versions before 1.24_02 for Perl parse the trailer in quadratic time.\n\nEverything after the last chunk in the same call to add() is parsed with HTTP::Headers, which takes time quadratic in the number of fields of one name.  For example, it takes several seconds to parse 16 KiB of \"a:\" lines.\n\nA remote attackercan exhause the CPU with a single request.\n\nHTTP::Body version 1.25 limits the size and number of lines in the trailer.",
  "severity": [
